- What changes if the input is already sorted or nearly sorted?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design incremental single-source shortest paths with batch updates and to reason about amortized work and practical data structures.

## Key Concepts
- Incremental SSSP with batch edge insertions
- Localized relaxation and pruning
- Priority queues and potential bucketed variants (Dial's)
- Amortized analysis and space efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
function updateBatch(batchEdges){
  for (const [u,v,w] of batchEdges){
    // ensure undirected view if needed
    adj[u].push([v,w]);
    adj[v].push([u,w]);
  }
  for (const [u,v,w] of batchEdges){
    if (dist[v] > dist[u] + w){
      dist[v] = dist[u] + w;
      pq.push([dist[v], v]);
    }
    if (dist[u] > dist[v] + w){
      dist[u] = dist[v] + w;
      pq.push([dist[u], u]);
    }
  }
  while (!pq.isEmpty()){
    const [d, x] = pq.pop();
    if (d !== dist[x]) continue;
    for (const [y,w] of adj[x]){
      if (dist[y] > dist[x] + w){
        dist[y] = dist[x] + w;
        pq.push([dist[y], y]);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked\n\nTests understanding of streaming frequency estimation under tight memory. The MG approach gives a bounded-memory alternative to exact counts, with concrete guarantees and practical trade-offs in real-time systems.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- Streaming algorithms, Misra-Gries, bounded counters, frequency estimation, error bounds, exact vs. approximate modes.\n- Trade-offs: k vs accuracy, batch size B vs throughput.\n\n## Code Example\n```javascript
class MGMode {
  constructor(k){
    this.k = k;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  add(x){
    if (this.counters.has(x)) this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x)+1);
    else if (this.counters.size < this.k) this.counters.set(x,1);
    else {
      for (const key of Array.from(this.counters.keys()))
        this.counters.set(key, this.counters.get(key)-1);
      for (const [key,c] of Array.from(this.counters))
        if (c<=0) this.counters.delete(key);
    }
  }
  estimate(){
    let best = null, bestc = -1;
    for (const [k,c] of this.counters) if (c>bestc){ bestc=c; best=k; }
    return best;
  }
}
```

